From 6760bc570fbf540c5dcb9ed192e2f4cadfa0db8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:40:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 91/91] Outposts can be besieged and taken

Outposts and the NPC conquerable stations in claimable space follow the
Dominion rules. If the owner's alliance holds sovereignty in the system
they can only be shot while the claim is under SBU blockade, and they get
two reinforcement timers: at 25% shield (out at 0% shield) and at 50%
armor (out at 25% armor). Each ends at the owner's exit time from station
management (noon by default) plus 48 hours, give or take 3 hours. Any
other outpost can be shot at any time and has no timers. At 0% structure
the station goes to the corporation of the last pilot to damage it.

- hit points come from the station types (100m/150m/100m)
- shields regenerate, also while the system is unloaded
- siege state is saved in staStationSiege (new migration)
- slim items carry structureState for the client's reinforcement effects
- the owner gets StationAggression2 alerts (hourly, and on reinforcement)
  and both corps get StationConquer
- outposts now have a target manager; locking one crashed before
- station attribute changes are no longer multicast to the owning corp
- GM: /sov siege [info|next|repair] [stationID], /sov complete ends a
  reinforcement
